      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Adding `FP_MODE_ENROLL_IMAGE` to this mask introduces regressions in the `fp_set_sensor_mode` validation logic (`chromium/common/fpsensor/fpsensor_state.cc`):\n\n1. **Breaks combined requests**: The host often sends `FP_MODE_ENROLL_SESSION | FP_MODE_ENROLL_IMAGE` together (as seen in `chromium/test/fpsensor_auth_commands.cc`). Because both are now in this mask, `std::popcount(mode \u0026 FP_MODES_WITH_AUTHENTICATION) \u003e 1` will evaluate to `true` and the request will be incorrectly rejected with `EC_ERROR_INVAL`.\n2. **Missing auth handler**: If `FP_MODE_ENROLL_IMAGE` is sent alone, the code will pass the popcount check, but fall through the `if (flags_enabled \u0026 FP_MODE_ENROLL_SESSION)` and `else if (flags_enabled \u0026 FP_MODE_MATCH)` block, ultimately returning `EC_ERROR_UNKNOWN`.\n\nYou must update the validation logic and authentication dispatch block in `fp_set_sensor_mode` to properly handle this new authenticated mode.",
